Write professional_summary in English as one natural sentence within the supplied character and line limits, counting spaces and punctuation.

Synthesize the candidate's professional profile from the assembled CV and declared skills. Choose one or two coherent areas of competence or approaches that are particularly relevant to the offer, without trying to cover the entire background.

Experiences and projects substantiate this synthesis: do not copy their descriptions or center the summary on an isolated task, achievement or use case. Express the transferable competencies actually exercised. Retain a sector-specific context only when it strengthens relevance to the offer.

Adapt the choice and emphasis of the competencies presented to the role's priorities. Do not turn offer requirements into candidate capabilities. A declared competence does not require citing an achievement; every specific attribution and generalization must preserve the scope of the available facts.

Stay consistent with cv_title without mechanically repeating it. Describe the profile directly, without commenting on its alignment with the offer. Use clear, fluent language accessible to a non-specialist recruiter, without "I", generic self-praise or a keyword inventory.

Do not mention any framework or library, even if present in the profile or offer. Do not include any numbers, percentages or quantified results. These prohibitions also apply to rewrites and review of the summary.

Prioritize precision over accumulation. A shorter summary is acceptable. Rephrase if necessary, but never truncate the text or remove a qualification essential to factual accuracy.

Writing or revising the summary must not change any other CV section. For the summary, these rules take precedence over general instructions to display technologies or include metrics.
